{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Be exalted.</b> The sense: \"I will sing among the peoples,\" and this is my song, that I make known that your steadfast love is great above the heavens, and you are Elohim — show that you are exalted above the heavens by delivering me. Therefore after it: \"so that.\" The rest of the psalm I have interpreted in the psalm \"upon Shoshannim Eduth,\" and it is in Psalm 60."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 108, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:09.752520355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}